                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A good puzzle-platformer game.\n\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1514547085\nI started playing this game and wanted to close it as soon as possible because there were not a tutorial, so I just couldn't realize what I need to do. After I got it, I liked the game much.\n\nThere are 6 world. Each world introduces new mechanics. You start with movement. Move left, Move Right and Jump moves blocks. You need to realize which block affect special movement and use it to pass the level.\n\nSecond world gives Checkpoint mechanics. You can activate it and start the level from this point.\nThird level gives Reset mechanics. To start the level clean, because Checkpoint mechanics doesn't reset certain blocks.\nFourth world gives and ability to shoot. Fire/Kill mobs to trigger certain situations\nFifth level allows a projectile to bounce.\nThe final world gives an ability to swap your character with an enemy.\n\nThe game could be passed in an hour. I think it's a great pros. \nI can recommend this game, because I passed it and liked playing.\n\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1514547012\nPros\n- A lot of fresh mechanics in the genre\n- Puzzles are diverse\n- Colorful worlds\n- The game is short. Could be finished in 1-1.5 hours\n\nCons\n- No tutorial. First impressions was strongly negative due confusing factor. I just didn't understand what I need to do and it drove me mad!\n\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1514547145\n[h1]Resume[/h1]\nA great Puzzle-Platformer game with a lot of fresh mechanics. Also, I liked much that it is short. The price is slightly overpriced for 1 hour game, so take it with a discount.",
